{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"text"},{"type":"text","value":" annotates scaled positions, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"frame"},{"type":"text","value":" paints the resolved inner chart\nbounds, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"facet"},{"type":"text","value":" composes complete child specs into responsive small\nmultiples."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { facet, facetChart, frame, lineY, text } from '@tanstack/charts'","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"text","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"text"}]},{"type":"code","value":"text(rows, {\n  x: 'date',\n  y: 'value',\n  text: 'label',\n  z: 'series',\n  dy: -8,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"function text<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options?: TextOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum, InferredX, InferredY>","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Meaning"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Layer-derived"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stable mark ID"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, ChartValue?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Row index"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Horizontal anchor"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, ChartValue?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Numeric datum"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vertical anchor"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"text"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, string | number?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"String form of datum"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Label content"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"z"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No group"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interaction group"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"color"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"z"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Value sent to the chart color scale"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"key"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, ChartKey>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ID, x, y, x/y, index"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stable identity"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fill"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VisualChannel<TDatum, string>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Theme foreground or resolved color"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Final label paint override"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fontSize"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inherited SVG font size"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Font size"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fontWeight"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inherited weight"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Numeric font weight"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"anchor"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VisualChannel<TDatum, TextAnchor>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'middle'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'start'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'middle'"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'end'"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rotate"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VisualChannel<TDatum, number>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No transform"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rotation in degrees around the final label origin"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dx"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VisualChannel<TDatum, number>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Horizontal pixel offset"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dy"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VisualChannel<TDatum, number>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vertical pixel offset"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"states"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"readonly ChartMarkState[]"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Focus-driven presentation overrides"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Labels use a middle baseline. Null or undefined text skips the row; the default\nfor a null datum is an empty string. Invalid x/y values also skip the row."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The interaction point is at the offset label origin. Its semantic values remain\nthe original x/y channels. Without an explicit key, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"text"},{"type":"text","value":" tries a unique\ntop-level or nested "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data.id"},{"type":"text","value":", then x, y, and the x/y tuple. Supply "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"key"},{"type":"text","value":" when\npositions can change while the same label should reconcile across updates."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"frame","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"frame"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"frame"},{"type":"text","value":" draws a background, border, or both around the final inner chart\nbounds:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"frame({\n  fill: 'color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 3%, transparent)',\n  strokeOpacity: 0.25,\n  radius: 8,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"function frame(options?: FrameOptions): ChartMark<never, never, never>","lang":"ts"},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Meaning"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Layer-derived"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stable mark ID"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fill"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'none'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Constant fill"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fillOpacity"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SVG default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fill opacity"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stroke"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Theme foreground"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Constant stroke"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeOpacity"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0.35"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stroke opacity"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeWidth"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stroke width"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inset"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pixels removed from all chart-bound edges; clamped to at least zero"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"radius"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Corner radius"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"frame"},{"type":"text","value":" materializes no scale channels and emits no interaction points. Put it\nbefore data marks when it should paint behind them."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"facet","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"facet"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"facet"},{"type":"text","value":" groups source rows by a key and renders one complete child chart spec\nper group inside the parent chart bounds."}]},{"type":"code","value":"facet(rows, {\n  by: 'region',\n  columns: 3,\n  minWidth: 220,\n  gap: 16,\n  label: (region) => `Region: ${region}`,\n  chart(groupRows) {\n    return {\n      marks: [lineY(groupRows, { x: 'date', y: 'value' })],\n      scales: {\n        x: { scale: makeXScale(groupRows) },\n        y: { scale: makeYScale(groupRows), grid: true },\n      },\n    }\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"function facet<TDatum, TChildSpec extends ChartSpec>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: FacetOptions<TDatum, TChildSpec>,\n): ChartMark<ChartSpecDatum<TChildSpec>>","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Meaning"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Layer-derived"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stable outer mark ID"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"by"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, ChartKey>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"String or number grouping key"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chart"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(data: readonly [TDatum, ...TDatum[]], context: FacetChartContext) => TChildSpec"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Builds one static child spec from a nonempty group"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columns"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Automatic"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Requested column count, floored and clamped to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1..groupCount"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"minWidth"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"220"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Target minimum cell width used for automatic columns"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gap"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"16"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gap between rows and columns, clamped to at least zero"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"label"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean | ((key) => string)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shows default key labels, formats them, or disables labels"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"axes"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'outer' | 'cell'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'outer'"},{"type":"text","value":" where shareable"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shared outside axes or independent axes in every cell"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"motion"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartMotionDefinition<ChartSpecDatum<TChildSpec>>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Motion policy over child-mark data"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FacetChartContext.key"},{"type":"text","value":" is the materialized value for the current group."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Facet preserves first-seen group order and original row order within each\ngroup. Non-string and non-number "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"by"},{"type":"text","value":" results are skipped."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Automatic columns are:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"floor((availableWidth + gap) / (minWidth + gap))","lang":"text"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"with a minimum of one. Rows are then derived from group count. Visible facet\nlabels reserve 22 pixels above every child plot."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"outer-axes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Outer axes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With more than one child and guides enabled, the default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"axes: 'outer'"},{"type":"text","value":"\nrenders y ticks on the first column, x ticks on the final occupied row, and\none shared title per dimension."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Outer axes require compatible cells:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"x and y resolved scale types, domains, ticks, labels, and direction match"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"axis label, label offset, and tick rotation match"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"foreground and muted theme tokens match"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"no child provides its own "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"margin"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"no child provides a color legend"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"no child sets "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"guides: false"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An incompatible facet throws with guidance to use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"axes: 'cell'"},{"type":"text","value":". This\nfail-fast behavior prevents a shared axis from implying a comparison the child\nscales do not support."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When every child sets "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"guides: false"},{"type":"text","value":", or there is only one child, facet uses\nthe cell rendering path even if "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"axes"},{"type":"text","value":" is omitted."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"cell-axes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cell axes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"axes: 'cell'"},{"type":"text","value":" when groups need independent scales, guide options, margins,\nor legends:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"facet(rows, {\n  by: 'region',\n  axes: 'cell',\n  chart: (groupRows) => buildIndependentSpec(groupRows),\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every child compiles at its own cell dimensions with the parent's text\nmeasurement. Compilation errors are wrapped with the facet and cell key."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"interaction","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interaction"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Child "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartPoint"},{"type":"text","value":" coordinates are offset into the parent scene. Point keys are\nprefixed with facet and group identity, so equal child keys remain unique\nacross cells. Datum, semantic x/y values, group, group label, and paint are\npreserved. The facet's output datum type comes from the marks returned by\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chart"},{"type":"text","value":"; grouping rows do not replace a child point's original datum. Motion\ncallbacks receive that same child datum type."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The facet mark itself has intentionally opaque positional types because each\nchild may return a different mark composition. Its child scale domains do not\nparticipate in the parent x/y scales."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"facetchart","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"facetChart"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"facetChart"},{"type":"text","value":" wraps a facet mark in a complete static definition:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const definition = facetChart(rows, {\n  by: 'region',\n  chart: (groupRows) => buildSpec(groupRows),\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"function facetChart<TDatum, TChildSpec extends ChartSpec>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: FacetOptions<TDatum, TChildSpec>,\n): StaticChartDefinition<ChartSpecDatum<TChildSpec>>","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The wrapper sets:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const specification = {\n  marks: [facet(source, options)],\n  margin: 0,\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"facet"},{"type":"text","value":" directly when the small multiples must be layered with other\nparent-scene marks. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"facetChart"},{"type":"text","value":" for the usual standalone chart."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"text","text":"text","level":2},{"id":"options","text":"Options","level":3},{"id":"frame","text":"frame","level":2},{"id":"facet","text":"facet","level":2},{"id":"options-2","text":"Options","level":3},{"id":"outer-axes","text":"Outer axes","level":3},{"id":"cell-axes","text":"Cell axes","level":3},{"id":"interaction","text":"Interaction","level":3},{"id":"facetchart","text":"facetChart","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n`text` annotates scaled positions, `frame` paints the resolved inner chart\nbounds, and `facet` composes complete child specs into responsive small\nmultiples.\n\n```ts\nimport { facet, facetChart, frame, lineY, text } from '@tanstack/charts'\n```\n\n## `text`\n\n```ts\ntext(rows, {\n  x: 'date',\n  y: 'value',\n  text: 'label',\n  z: 'series',\n  dy: -8,\n})\n```\n\n```ts\nfunction text<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options?: TextOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum, InferredX, InferredY>\n```\n\n### Options\n\n| Option       | Type                                 | Default                            | Meaning                                           |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `id`         | `string`                             | Layer-derived                      | Stable mark ID                                    |\n| `x`          | `Channel<TDatum, ChartValue?>`       | Row index                          | Horizontal anchor                                 |\n| `y`          | `Channel<TDatum, ChartValue?>`       | Numeric datum                      | Vertical anchor                                   |\n| `text`       | `Channel<TDatum, string \\| number?>` | String form of datum               | Label content                                     |\n| `z`          | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`         | No group                           | Interaction group                                 |\n| `color`      | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`         | `z`                                | Value sent to the chart color scale               |\n| `key`        | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey>`          | ID, x, y, x/y, index               | Stable identity                                   |\n| `fill`       | `VisualChannel<TDatum, string>`      | Theme foreground or resolved color | Final label paint override                        |\n| `fontSize`   | `number`                             | Inherited SVG font size            | Font size                                         |\n| `fontWeight` | `number`                             | Inherited weight                   | Numeric font weight                               |\n| `anchor`     | `VisualChannel<TDatum, TextAnchor>`  | `'middle'`                         | `'start'`, `'middle'`, or `'end'`                 |\n| `rotate`     | `VisualChannel<TDatum, number>`      | No transform                       | Rotation in degrees around the final label origin |\n| `dx`         | `VisualChannel<TDatum, number>`      | `0`                                | Horizontal pixel offset                           |\n| `dy`         | `VisualChannel<TDatum, number>`      | `0`                                | Vertical pixel offset                             |\n| `states`     | `readonly ChartMarkState[]`          | None                               | Focus-driven presentation overrides               |\n\nLabels use a middle baseline. Null or undefined text skips the row; the default\nfor a null datum is an empty string. Invalid x/y values also skip the row.\n\nThe interaction point is at the offset label origin. Its semantic values remain\nthe original x/y channels. Without an explicit key, `text` tries a unique\ntop-level or nested `data.id`, then x, y, and the x/y tuple. Supply `key` when\npositions can change while the same label should reconcile across updates.\n\n## `frame`\n\n`frame` draws a background, border, or both around the final inner chart\nbounds:\n\n```ts\nframe({\n  fill: 'color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 3%, transparent)',\n  strokeOpacity: 0.25,\n  radius: 8,\n})\n```\n\n```ts\nfunction frame(options?: FrameOptions): ChartMark<never, never, never>\n```\n\n| Option          | Type     | Default          | Meaning                                                             |\n| --------------- | -------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `id`            | `string` | Layer-derived    | Stable mark ID                                                      |\n| `fill`          | `string` | `'none'`         | Constant fill                                                       |\n| `fillOpacity`   | `number` | SVG default      | Fill opacity                                                        |\n| `stroke`        | `string` | Theme foreground | Constant stroke                                                     |\n| `strokeOpacity` | `number` | `0.35`           | Stroke opacity                                                      |\n| `strokeWidth`   | `number` | `1`              | Stroke width                                                        |\n| `inset`         | `number` | `0`              | Pixels removed from all chart-bound edges; clamped to at least zero |\n| `radius`        | `number` | None             | Corner radius                                                       |\n\n`frame` materializes no scale channels and emits no interaction points. Put it\nbefore data marks when it should paint behind them.\n\n## `facet`\n\n`facet` groups source rows by a key and renders one complete child chart spec\nper group inside the parent chart bounds.\n\n```ts\nfacet(rows, {\n  by: 'region',\n  columns: 3,\n  minWidth: 220,\n  gap: 16,\n  label: (region) => `Region: ${region}`,\n  chart(groupRows) {\n    return {\n      marks: [lineY(groupRows, { x: 'date', y: 'value' })],\n      scales: {\n        x: { scale: makeXScale(groupRows) },\n        y: { scale: makeYScale(groupRows), grid: true },\n      },\n    }\n  },\n})\n```\n\n```ts\nfunction facet<TDatum, TChildSpec extends ChartSpec>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: FacetOptions<TDatum, TChildSpec>,\n): ChartMark<ChartSpecDatum<TChildSpec>>\n```\n\n### Options\n\n| Option     | Type                                                                               | Default                   | Meaning                                                        |\n| ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `id`       | `string`                                                                           | Layer-derived             | Stable outer mark ID                                           |\n| `by`       | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey>`                                                        | Required                  | String or number grouping key                                  |\n| `chart`    | `(data: readonly [TDatum, ...TDatum[]], context: FacetChartContext) => TChildSpec` | Required                  | Builds one static child spec from a nonempty group             |\n| `columns`  | `number`                                                                           | Automatic                 | Requested column count, floored and clamped to `1..groupCount` |\n| `minWidth` | `number`                                                                           | `220`                     | Target minimum cell width used for automatic columns           |\n| `gap`      | `number`                                                                           | `16`                      | Gap between rows and columns, clamped to at least zero         |\n| `label`    | `boolean \\| ((key) => string)`                                                     | `true`                    | Shows default key labels, formats them, or disables labels     |\n| `axes`     | `'outer' \\| 'cell'`                                                                | `'outer'` where shareable | Shared outside axes or independent axes in every cell          |\n| `motion`   | `ChartMotionDefinition<ChartSpecDatum<TChildSpec>>`                                | None                      | Motion policy over child-mark data                             |\n\n`FacetChartContext.key` is the materialized value for the current group.\n\nFacet preserves first-seen group order and original row order within each\ngroup. Non-string and non-number `by` results are skipped.\n\nAutomatic columns are:\n\n```text\nfloor((availableWidth + gap) / (minWidth + gap))\n```\n\nwith a minimum of one. Rows are then derived from group count. Visible facet\nlabels reserve 22 pixels above every child plot.\n\n### Outer axes\n\nWith more than one child and guides enabled, the default `axes: 'outer'`\nrenders y ticks on the first column, x ticks on the final occupied row, and\none shared title per dimension.\n\nOuter axes require compatible cells:\n\n- x and y resolved scale types, domains, ticks, labels, and direction match\n- axis label, label offset, and tick rotation match\n- foreground and muted theme tokens match\n- no child provides its own `margin`\n- no child provides a color legend\n- no child sets `guides: false`\n\nAn incompatible facet throws with guidance to use `axes: 'cell'`. This\nfail-fast behavior prevents a shared axis from implying a comparison the child\nscales do not support.\n\nWhen every child sets `guides: false`, or there is only one child, facet uses\nthe cell rendering path even if `axes` is omitted.\n\n### Cell axes\n\nSet `axes: 'cell'` when groups need independent scales, guide options, margins,\nor legends:\n\n```ts\nfacet(rows, {\n  by: 'region',\n  axes: 'cell',\n  chart: (groupRows) => buildIndependentSpec(groupRows),\n})\n```\n\nEvery child compiles at its own cell dimensions with the parent's text\nmeasurement. Compilation errors are wrapped with the facet and cell key.\n\n### Interaction\n\nChild `ChartPoint` coordinates are offset into the parent scene. Point keys are\nprefixed with facet and group identity, so equal child keys remain unique\nacross cells. Datum, semantic x/y values, group, group label, and paint are\npreserved. The facet's output datum type comes from the marks returned by\n`chart`; grouping rows do not replace a child point's original datum. Motion\ncallbacks receive that same child datum type.\n\nThe facet mark itself has intentionally opaque positional types because each\nchild may return a different mark composition. Its child scale domains do not\nparticipate in the parent x/y scales.\n\n## `facetChart`\n\n`facetChart` wraps a facet mark in a complete static definition:\n\n```ts\nconst definition = facetChart(rows, {\n  by: 'region',\n  chart: (groupRows) => buildSpec(groupRows),\n})\n```\n\n```ts\nfunction facetChart<TDatum, TChildSpec extends ChartSpec>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: FacetOptions<TDatum, TChildSpec>,\n): StaticChartDefinition<ChartSpecDatum<TChildSpec>>\n```\n\nThe wrapper sets:\n\n```ts\nconst specification = {\n  marks: [facet(source, options)],\n  margin: 0,\n}\n```\n\nUse `facet` directly when the small multiples must be layered with other\nparent-scene marks. Use `facetChart` for the usual standalone chart.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Text, Frame, and Facet Marks\ndescription: Reference for data labels, chart frames, responsive small multiples, shared or per-cell axes, labels, and facet constraints.\n---\n\n`text` annotates scaled positions, `frame` paints the resolved inner chart\nbounds, and `facet` composes complete child specs into responsive small\nmultiples.\n\n```ts\nimport { facet, facetChart, frame, lineY, text } from '@tanstack/charts'\n```\n\n## `text`\n\n```ts\ntext(rows, {\n  x: 'date',\n  y: 'value',\n  text: 'label',\n  z: 'series',\n  dy: -8,\n})\n```\n\n```ts\nfunction text<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options?: TextOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum, InferredX, InferredY>\n```\n\n### Options\n\n| Option       | Type                                 | Default                            | Meaning                                           |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `id`         | `string`                             | Layer-derived                      | Stable mark ID                                    |\n| `x`          | `Channel<TDatum, ChartValue?>`       | Row index                          | Horizontal anchor                                 |\n| `y`          | `Channel<TDatum, ChartValue?>`       | Numeric datum                      | Vertical anchor                                   |\n| `text`       | `Channel<TDatum, string \\| number?>` | String form of datum               | Label content                                     |\n| `z`          | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`         | No group                           | Interaction group                                 |\n| `color`      | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`         | `z`                                | Value sent to the chart color scale               |\n| `key`        | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey>`          | ID, x, y, x/y, index               | Stable identity                                   |\n| `fill`       | `VisualChannel<TDatum, string>`      | Theme foreground or resolved color | Final label paint override                        |\n| `fontSize`   | `number`                             | Inherited SVG font size            | Font size                                         |\n| `fontWeight` | `number`                             | Inherited weight                   | Numeric font weight                               |\n| `anchor`     | `VisualChannel<TDatum, TextAnchor>`  | `'middle'`                         | `'start'`, `'middle'`, or `'end'`                 |\n| `rotate`     | `VisualChannel<TDatum, number>`      | No transform                       | Rotation in degrees around the final label origin |\n| `dx`         | `VisualChannel<TDatum, number>`      | `0`                                | Horizontal pixel offset                           |\n| `dy`         | `VisualChannel<TDatum, number>`      | `0`                                | Vertical pixel offset                             |\n| `states`     | `readonly ChartMarkState[]`          | None                               | Focus-driven presentation overrides               |\n\nLabels use a middle baseline. Null or undefined text skips the row; the default\nfor a null datum is an empty string. Invalid x/y values also skip the row.\n\nThe interaction point is at the offset label origin. Its semantic values remain\nthe original x/y channels. Without an explicit key, `text` tries a unique\ntop-level or nested `data.id`, then x, y, and the x/y tuple. Supply `key` when\npositions can change while the same label should reconcile across updates.\n\n## `frame`\n\n`frame` draws a background, border, or both around the final inner chart\nbounds:\n\n```ts\nframe({\n  fill: 'color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 3%, transparent)',\n  strokeOpacity: 0.25,\n  radius: 8,\n})\n```\n\n```ts\nfunction frame(options?: FrameOptions): ChartMark<never, never, never>\n```\n\n| Option          | Type     | Default          | Meaning                                                             |\n| --------------- | -------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `id`            | `string` | Layer-derived    | Stable mark ID                                                      |\n| `fill`          | `string` | `'none'`         | Constant fill                                                       |\n| `fillOpacity`   | `number` | SVG default      | Fill opacity                                                        |\n| `stroke`        | `string` | Theme foreground | Constant stroke                                                     |\n| `strokeOpacity` | `number` | `0.35`           | Stroke opacity                                                      |\n| `strokeWidth`   | `number` | `1`              | Stroke width                                                        |\n| `inset`         | `number` | `0`              | Pixels removed from all chart-bound edges; clamped to at least zero |\n| `radius`        | `number` | None             | Corner radius                                                       |\n\n`frame` materializes no scale channels and emits no interaction points. Put it\nbefore data marks when it should paint behind them.\n\n## `facet`\n\n`facet` groups source rows by a key and renders one complete child chart spec\nper group inside the parent chart bounds.\n\n```ts\nfacet(rows, {\n  by: 'region',\n  columns: 3,\n  minWidth: 220,\n  gap: 16,\n  label: (region) => `Region: ${region}`,\n  chart(groupRows) {\n    return {\n      marks: [lineY(groupRows, { x: 'date', y: 'value' })],\n      scales: {\n        x: { scale: makeXScale(groupRows) },\n        y: { scale: makeYScale(groupRows), grid: true },\n      },\n    }\n  },\n})\n```\n\n```ts\nfunction facet<TDatum, TChildSpec extends ChartSpec>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: FacetOptions<TDatum, TChildSpec>,\n): ChartMark<ChartSpecDatum<TChildSpec>>\n```\n\n### Options\n\n| Option     | Type                                                                               | Default                   | Meaning                                                        |\n| ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `id`       | `string`                                                                           | Layer-derived             | Stable outer mark ID                                           |\n| `by`       | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey>`                                                        | Required                  | String or number grouping key                                  |\n| `chart`    | `(data: readonly [TDatum, ...TDatum[]], context: FacetChartContext) => TChildSpec` | Required                  | Builds one static child spec from a nonempty group             |\n| `columns`  | `number`                                                                           | Automatic                 | Requested column count, floored and clamped to `1..groupCount` |\n| `minWidth` | `number`                                                                           | `220`                     | Target minimum cell width used for automatic columns           |\n| `gap`      | `number`                                                                           | `16`                      | Gap between rows and columns, clamped to at least zero         |\n| `label`    | `boolean \\| ((key) => string)`                                                     | `true`                    | Shows default key labels, formats them, or disables labels     |\n| `axes`     | `'outer' \\| 'cell'`                                                                | `'outer'` where shareable | Shared outside axes or independent axes in every cell          |\n| `motion`   | `ChartMotionDefinition<ChartSpecDatum<TChildSpec>>`                                | None                      | Motion policy over child-mark data                             |\n\n`FacetChartContext.key` is the materialized value for the current group.\n\nFacet preserves first-seen group order and original row order within each\ngroup. Non-string and non-number `by` results are skipped.\n\nAutomatic columns are:\n\n```text\nfloor((availableWidth + gap) / (minWidth + gap))\n```\n\nwith a minimum of one. Rows are then derived from group count. Visible facet\nlabels reserve 22 pixels above every child plot.\n\n### Outer axes\n\nWith more than one child and guides enabled, the default `axes: 'outer'`\nrenders y ticks on the first column, x ticks on the final occupied row, and\none shared title per dimension.\n\nOuter axes require compatible cells:\n\n- x and y resolved scale types, domains, ticks, labels, and direction match\n- axis label, label offset, and tick rotation match\n- foreground and muted theme tokens match\n- no child provides its own `margin`\n- no child provides a color legend\n- no child sets `guides: false`\n\nAn incompatible facet throws with guidance to use `axes: 'cell'`. This\nfail-fast behavior prevents a shared axis from implying a comparison the child\nscales do not support.\n\nWhen every child sets `guides: false`, or there is only one child, facet uses\nthe cell rendering path even if `axes` is omitted.\n\n### Cell axes\n\nSet `axes: 'cell'` when groups need independent scales, guide options, margins,\nor legends:\n\n```ts\nfacet(rows, {\n  by: 'region',\n  axes: 'cell',\n  chart: (groupRows) => buildIndependentSpec(groupRows),\n})\n```\n\nEvery child compiles at its own cell dimensions with the parent's text\nmeasurement. Compilation errors are wrapped with the facet and cell key.\n\n### Interaction\n\nChild `ChartPoint` coordinates are offset into the parent scene. Point keys are\nprefixed with facet and group identity, so equal child keys remain unique\nacross cells. Datum, semantic x/y values, group, group label, and paint are\npreserved. The facet's output datum type comes from the marks returned by\n`chart`; grouping rows do not replace a child point's original datum. Motion\ncallbacks receive that same child datum type.\n\nThe facet mark itself has intentionally opaque positional types because each\nchild may return a different mark composition. Its child scale domains do not\nparticipate in the parent x/y scales.\n\n## `facetChart`\n\n`facetChart` wraps a facet mark in a complete static definition:\n\n```ts\nconst definition = facetChart(rows, {\n  by: 'region',\n  chart: (groupRows) => buildSpec(groupRows),\n})\n```\n\n```ts\nfunction facetChart<TDatum, TChildSpec extends ChartSpec>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: FacetOptions<TDatum, TChildSpec>,\n): StaticChartDefinition<ChartSpecDatum<TChildSpec>>\n```\n\nThe wrapper sets:\n\n```ts\nconst specification = {\n  marks: [facet(source, options)],\n  margin: 0,\n}\n```\n\nUse `facet` directly when the small multiples must be layered with other\nparent-scene marks. Use `facetChart` for the usual standalone chart.\n"}
